            <ArticleTitle>[Prolonged peridural block for postoperative analgesia in heart surgery patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prolonged peridural blockade with trimekain used in 1000 cardiosurgical patients is shown to be an effective prophylactic measure against postoperative complications. This method should not be widely used in patients with blood circulation insufficiency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
